//RS /// `jet fix --edition=2027` rewrites `json.canonical(x)` per D-JSONCANON1:
//RS /// an omitted contract is the implicit default `Err`, so a fallible function
//RS /// keeps `json.canonical(x)` and propagates automatically, while a `Never!`
//RS /// function gets `json.canonical(x) ?? panic("value is not canonical JSON")`.
//RS /// A re-run must be a no-op (idempotent), including when the existing
//RS /// fallback already has a space before `??` (the bug that made `jet fix`
//RS /// double-append the panic fallback on every re-run).
//RS #[test]
//RS fn jet_fix_edition_2027_rewrites_json_canonical_and_is_idempotent() {
